{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LTpGua7h1k2HKfjWarCjeh","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 0c699f47db37c003275f29864448c5df4456a5d9\nAuthor: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>\nDate:   Mon Apr 13 16:08:46 2026 +0200\n\n    Batch Round 0 descriptor arrays: CUDA kernels, FFI, and Rust batch helpers (infrastructure)\n    \n    Add batched descriptor-array kernels for Round 0 zerocheck constraint evaluation\n    and logup interaction evaluation. This is infrastructure-only: the kernels compile\n    and link but are not yet wired into the proving pipeline.\n    \n    CUDA changes:\n    - Round0ZcCtx/Round0LogupCtx per-AIR descriptor structs\n    - batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel: 1D grid, each block reads BlockCtx\n      to find its AIR and (coset, x_block) indices\n    - batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel: same pattern with identity-coset handling\n    - Extern \"C\" launchers with batched_final_reduce_block_sums reduction\n    \n    Rust changes:\n    - #[repr(C)] FFI structs and safe wrapper functions\n    - BatchedR0AirDesc, BatchedR0LogupRules descriptor types\n    - build_logup_rules_for_air() for pre-building DAG rules\n    - evaluate_batched_zerocheck_group() and evaluate_batched_logup_group()\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .../cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu       | 239 ++++++++++++++\n .../cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu   | 236 ++++++++++++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs    | 141 +++++++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs  | 345 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n 4 files changed, 959 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e3c2c89-9ba9-4e03-a0d9-bb2105990b3b","uuid":"3c6c1a73-90f5-443f-809c-1b5f3a09ef6d","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:38:11.649Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 0c699f47db37c003275f29864448c5df4456a5d9\nAuthor: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>\nDate:   Mon Apr 13 16:08:46 2026 +0200\n\n    Batch Round 0 descriptor arrays: CUDA kernels, FFI, and Rust batch helpers (infrastructure)\n    \n    Add batched descriptor-array kernels for Round 0 zerocheck constraint evaluation\n    and logup interaction evaluation. This is infrastructure-only: the kernels compile\n    and link but are not yet wired into the proving pipeline.\n    \n    CUDA changes:\n    - Round0ZcCtx/Round0LogupCtx per-AIR descriptor structs\n    - batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel: 1D grid, each block reads BlockCtx\n      to find its AIR and (coset, x_block) indices\n    - batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel: same pattern with identity-coset handling\n    - Extern \"C\" launchers with batched_final_reduce_block_sums reduction\n    \n    Rust changes:\n    - #[repr(C)] FFI structs and safe wrapper functions\n    - BatchedR0AirDesc, BatchedR0LogupRules descriptor types\n    - build_logup_rules_for_air() for pre-building DAG rules\n    - evaluate_batched_zerocheck_group() and evaluate_batched_logup_group()\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .../cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu       | 239 ++++++++++++++\n .../cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu   | 236 ++++++++++++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs    | 141 +++++++++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs  | 345 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n 4 files changed, 959 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
