{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qvg3oiAS9YzXgf8XFJJTaP","type":"tool_result","content":"\u001b[1;32mINFO    \u001b[0m ｉ [info]: Generating STARK proof (app + aggregation)...\nthread 'main' (1981574) panicked at /home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/d_buffer.rs:68:44:\n\u001b[1;31mERROR   \u001b[0m             │     │  ┕━ 🚨 [error]: vpmm_create_physical failed: device=0, page_size=2097152: CudaError { code: 2, name: \"cudaErrorMemoryAllocation\", message: \"out of memory\" }\nShell cwd was reset to /home/georg/stark-backend","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e3c2c89-9ba9-4e03-a0d9-bb2105990b3b","uuid":"9828c6b4-56a1-44c9-abb3-22c0f6d86a0f","timestamp":"2026-04-13T15:51:04.067Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\u001b[1;32mINFO    \u001b[0m ｉ [info]: Generating STARK proof (app + aggregation)...\nthread 'main' (1981574) panicked at /home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/d_buffer.rs:68:44:\n\u001b[1;31mERROR   \u001b[0m             │     │  ┕━ 🚨 [error]: vpmm_create_physical failed: device=0, page_size=2097152: CudaError { code: 2, name: \"cudaErrorMemoryAllocation\", message: \"out of memory\" }","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/georg/stark-backend","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NVNq5KwRp1fVvWk8WWRc3e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still OOM but no stale processes. Let me check what the allocation request is. The script runs APC 300, 100, 0 in sequence. The first APC (300) seems to fail with OOM in gkr_input.\n\nBut wait — the before measurements show APC 300 worked fine. The difference is:\n1. Before: l_skip was probably 3 (based on the plan's analysis)\n2. The APC 100 test showed l_skip=4\n\nWait, l_skip=4 means skip_domain=16. \n\nThat's bigger than l_skip=3 (skip_domain=8). So the GKR input OOM with an 8GB allocation request is suspicious — could my batched code be allocating and not freeing memory before gkr_input runs? Actually no, looking at the code flow, GKR input evals run first before Round 0, so the batched code hasn't even executed when the OOM happens. This is a pre-existing issue I wasn't causing.\n\nBut wait, the before measurements succeeded, so something changed. Maybe the clean rebuild affected CUDA memory pool behavior, or perhaps the run_pairing.sh script leaves GPU garbage between runs. But the first run itself already fails with OOM on the 8GB allocation, so it's not a cascading issue. Let me compare the before measurement's l_skip value by checking its STARK trace time — it shows 1429ms for APC 300.\n\nNow I'm seeing Round 0 took 301ms with 623 AIR instances. The 8GB allocation request seems suspicious — I need to figure out if this is a regression from my changes or if it was already happening. The quickest way to test is to temporarily revert my changes to a no-op batched function and see if APC 300 passes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":219753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":327},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","i